<body>
    <h1>Security Validation</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <h2 id=3D"SecurityValidation-1.AllCommunicationsUseTLS">1. All Comm=
unications Use TLS</h2>
<ul>
<li>
<p>All plain HTTP requests are correctly rejected.</p></li>
<li>
<p>TLS handshakes complete successfully.</p></li>
<li>
<p>No plaintext ports are exposed.</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"SecurityValidation-1.1.HTTPPortProperlyRejected">1.1. HTTP Port P=
roperly Rejected</h3>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">curl ht=
tp://lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com:8500/
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Result</strong>: <code>400 Bad Request - Client sent HTTP to HTT=
PS server</code></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Plain HTTP is not accepted, as expected.</p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"SecurityValidation-1.2.HTTPSPortResponds">1.2. HTTPS Port Respond=
s</h3>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">curl ht=
tps://lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com:8500/
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Result</strong>: TLS handshake completes successfully (a certifi=
cate warning may appear due to hostname mismatch)</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Communication is encrypted with TLS.</p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"SecurityValidation-1.3.NoPlaintextPortsOpenforConsul">1.3. No Pla=
intext Ports Open for Consul</h3>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">netstat=
 -tulnp | grep consul
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Result</strong>: Only TLS-capable ports like <code>8301</code>, =
<code>8302</code>, and <code>8500</code> are open.</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>No unencrypted (plaintext) ports are listening.</p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"SecurityValidation-1.4.UIAccessVerification">1.4. UI Access Verif=
ication</h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Open browser: <code>https://10.161.244.15:8500/ui</code></p></li>
<li>
<p>Click "Advanced" =E2=86=92 "Proceed to site" (to bypass certificate warn=
ing)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Expected result: Consul UI loads successfully</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Status</strong>: UI is accessible only over HTTPS.</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Certificate warning exists due to hostname mismatch, but it <strong>does=
 not affect encryption or security</strong></p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"SecurityValidation-2.ServiceDiscoveryWorksOverSecureConnections">=
2. Service Discovery Works Over Secure Connections</h2>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Services can <strong>find each other</strong> through Consul</p></li>
<li>
<p>All discovery communications are <strong>encrypted</strong> (no plaintex=
t)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Services get correct connection info (hostnames, ports)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Everything works <strong>without any HTTP/unencrypted fallback</strong><=
/p></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"SecurityValidation-2.1.EnforceHTTPS-OnlyRegistration(UsingDomainN=
ame+CACert)">2.1. Enforce HTTPS-Only Registration (Using Domain Name + CA C=
ert)</h3>
<h3 id=3D"SecurityValidation-2.1.1.HTTPSRegistration(ShouldPass)">2.1.1. HT=
TPS Registration (Should Pass)</h3>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">curl --=
cacert /etc/letsencrypt/live/lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com/chain.pem -X PUT -=
d '{
  "ID": "test-https",
  "Name": "test-https",
  "Address": "lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com",
  "Port": 8080
}' "https://lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com:8500/v1/agent/service/register"
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Uses HTTPS and valid cert.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Service registered securely.</p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"SecurityValidation-2.1.2.HTTPonHTTPSPort(ShouldFail)">2.1.2. HTTP=
 on HTTPS Port (Should Fail)</h3>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">curl -k=
 -X PUT -d '{
  "ID": "test-http",
  "Name": "test-http",
  "Address": "lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com",
  "Port": 8080
}' "http://10.161.244.15:8500/v1/agent/service/register"
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>Expected Output:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">curl: (=
1) Received HTTP/0.9 when not allowed
Client sent an HTTP request to an HTTPS server.
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<ul>
<li>
<p><code>http://</code> used on a TLS-only port.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Protocol mismatch error =E2=80=94 registration blocked.</p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"SecurityValidation-2.2.TestingusingtwoFastAPIservices">2.2. Testi=
ng using two FastAPI services</h3>
<p>These are two FastAPI services running on ports <code>11003</code> and <=
code>11004</code>, built for testing service discovery. This approach can a=
lso be extended to any HTTPS service such as Metagen, Facial Recognition, e=
tc.</p>
<h3 id=3D"SecurityValidation-2.2.1ValidateServiceRegistration">2.2.1 Valida=
te Service Registration</h3>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># List =
all services (HTTPS only)
consul catalog services \
  -http-addr=3D"https://lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com:8500" \
  -ca-file=3D/etc/letsencrypt/live/lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com/chain.pem

# Check service details
curl --cacert /etc/letsencrypt/live/lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com/chain.pem \
  "https://lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com:8500/v1/catalog/service/service-a"
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"SecurityValidation-2.2.2TestServiceDiscoveryMechanisms">2.2.2 Tes=
t Service Discovery Mechanisms</h3>
<h4 id=3D"SecurityValidation-DNS-BasedDiscovery">DNS-Based Discovery</h4>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">dig @12=
7.0.0.1 -p 8600 service-a.service.consul +short
dig @127.0.0.1 -p 8600 service-b.service.consul +short
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"SecurityValidation-API-BasedDiscovery">API-Based Discovery</h4>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># From =
Service-A (discover Service-B)
curl --cacert /etc/letsencrypt/live/lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com/chain.pem  =
 "https://lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com:11004/discover-services?service_name=
=3Dservice-b"

# From Service-B (discover Service-A)
curl --cacert /etc/letsencrypt/live/lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com/chain.pem \
  "https://lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com:11003/discover-services?service_name=
=3Dservice-a"

# From Service-B (discover Consul)
curl --cacert /etc/letsencrypt/live/lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com/chain.pem \
  "https://lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com:11003/discover-services?service_name=
=3Dconsul"
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"SecurityValidation-2.2.3VerifyService-to-ServiceCommunication">2.=
2.3 Verify Service-to-Service Communication</h3>
<h4 id=3D"SecurityValidation-HTTPSCommunication(ShouldPass)">HTTPS Communic=
ation (Should Pass)</h4>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># Servi=
ce-A =E2=86=92 Service-B
curl --cacert /etc/letsencrypt/live/lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com/chain.pem \
  https://lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com:11003/health

# Service-B =E2=86=92 Service-A
curl --cacert /etc/letsencrypt/live/lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com/chain.pem \
  https://lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com:11004/health
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"SecurityValidation-HTTPCommunication(ShouldFail)">HTTP Communicat=
ion (Should Fail)</h4>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># Servi=
ce-A =E2=86=92 Service-B (HTTP)
curl http://lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com:11003/health

# Service-B =E2=86=92 Service-A (HTTP)
curl http://lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com:11004/health</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>Expected Output:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">curl: (=
52) Empty reply from server</pre>
</div>
</div>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"SecurityValidation-2.3.CertificateValidation">2.3. Certificate Va=
lidation</h3>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># Verif=
y Consul's certificate
openssl s_client -connect lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com:8500 \
  -CAfile /etc/letsencrypt/live/lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com/chain.pem

# Verify Service-A's certificate
openssl s_client -connect lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com:11004 \
  -CAfile /etc/letsencrypt/live/lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com/chain.pem
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"SecurityValidation-3.ConsulUIisAccessibleOnlyviaHTTPS"><strong>3.=
 Consul UI is Accessible Only via HTTPS</strong></h2>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Consul web interface <strong>cannot</strong> be accessed using <code=
>http://</code></p></li>
<li>
<p>All access must use <code>https://</code></p></li>
<li>
<p>Any attempt to use HTTP should automatically redirect to HTTPS or be blo=
cked</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"SecurityValidation-3.1.HTTPAccessisBlocked">3.1. HTTP Access is B=
locked</h3>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">curl ht=
tp://lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com:8500/ui
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Expected Output:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">HTTP/1.=
0 400 Bad Request
Client sent an HTTP request to an HTTPS server.
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Correct</strong>: Confirms that port <code>8500</code> is config=
ured to expect HTTPS only and rejects HTTP.</p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"SecurityValidation-3.2.HTTPSAccessWorks">3.2. HTTPS Access Works<=
/h3>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">curl ht=
tps://lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com:8500/ui
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Expected Output:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">&lt; HT=
TP/2 301
&lt; location: /ui/
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<ul>
<li>
<p>A <strong>successful TLS handshake</strong> occurs.</p></li>
<li>
<p>A <strong>301 redirect</strong> from <code>/ui</code> to <code>/ui/</cod=
e> is expected from Consul UI.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Certificate is valid (issued by <strong>Let=E2=80=99s Encrypt</strong> f=
or <code>lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com</code>).</p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"SecurityValidation-3.3.PortConfigurationLooksSecure">3.3. Port Co=
nfiguration Looks Secure</h3>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">netstat=
 -tulnp | grep consul
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Expected Output:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">tcp6 ::=
:8500 :::* LISTEN
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Only <strong>HTTPS port (8500)</strong> is open.</p></li>
<li>
<p>No unencrypted port exposed.</p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"SecurityValidation-3.4.BrowserTest">3.4. Browser Test</h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Navigating to <code>http://10.161.244.15:8500/ui</code> fails or trigger=
s a redirect.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Navigating to <code>https://10.161.244.15:8500/ui/</code> loads the Cons=
ul UI.</p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"SecurityValidation-4.Configurationchangespropagatecorrectlyoverse=
cureconnections">4.<strong>Configuration changes propagate correctly over s=
ecure connections</strong></h2>
<h3 id=3D"SecurityValidation-4.1.KVStoreSecurityTests"><strong>4.1. KV Stor=
e Security Tests</strong></h3>
<h3 id=3D"SecurityValidation-Write/ReadEncryptedData">Write/Read Encrypted =
Data</h3>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># Write=
 secure value
curl --cacert /etc/letsencrypt/live/lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com/chain.pem \
  -X PUT -d 'secure-value' \
  "https://lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com:8500/v1/kv/secure-test"

# Read back value
curl --cacert /etc/letsencrypt/live/lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com/chain.pem \
  "https://lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com:8500/v1/kv/secure-test?raw"
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Expected Results</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>PUT =E2=86=92 Returns <code>true</code></p></li>
<li>
<p>GET =E2=86=92 Returns <code>secure-value</code></p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"SecurityValidation-4.2.ServiceRegistrationSecurity"><strong>4.2. =
Service Registration Security</strong></h3>
<h3 id=3D"SecurityValidation-Register/VerifyHTTPSService">Register/Verify H=
TTPS Service</h3>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># Regis=
ter new service
curl --cacert /etc/letsencrypt/live/lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com/chain.pem \
  -X PUT -d '{
    "ID": "test-https",
    "Name": "test-https",
    "Address": "lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com",
    "Port": 8443,
    "Tags": ["https-only"]
  }' "https://lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com:8500/v1/agent/service/register"

# Verify registration
curl --cacert /etc/letsencrypt/live/lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com/chain.pem \
  "https://lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com:8500/v1/catalog/service/test-https" =
| jq
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Expected Results</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Returns JSON with service details including <code>"https-only"</code> ta=
g</p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"SecurityValidation-4.3.NegativeTests"><strong>4.3. Negative Tests=
 </strong></h3>
<h3 id=3D"SecurityValidation-AttemptUnencryptedOperations">Attempt Unencryp=
ted Operations</h3>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># Try H=
TTP service registration
curl -X PUT -d '{
  "ID": "test-http",
  "Name": "test-http",
  "Port": 8080
}' "http://lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com:8500/v1/agent/service/register"

# Try HTTP KV write
curl -X PUT -d 'insecure' "http://lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com:8500/v1/kv/in=
secure-test"
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Expected Results</strong>:</p>
<p>Both commands return:</p>
<p><code>Client sent an HTTP request to an HTTPS server</code></p>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"SecurityValidation-4.4.NetworkConfiguration"><strong>4.4. Network=
 Configuration</strong></h3>
<h3 id=3D"SecurityValidation-VerifyListeningPorts">Verify Listening Ports</=
h3>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">ss -tul=
np | grep -E '8300|8302'
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Expected Results</strong>:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">tcp  LI=
STEN 0 4096 10.161.244.15:8300 0.0.0.0:*  users:(("consul",pid=3DXXX,fd=3DX=
X))
tcp  LISTEN 0 4096 10.161.244.15:8302 0.0.0.0:*  users:(("consul",pid=3DXXX=
,fd=3DXX))
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"SecurityValidation-4.5.ConfigurationPersistence"><strong>4.5. Con=
figuration Persistence</strong></h3>
<h3 id=3D"SecurityValidation-TestReloadandPersistence">Test Reload and Pers=
istence</h3>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># Trigg=
er reload
curl --cacert /etc/letsencrypt/live/lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com/chain.pem \
  -X PUT "https://lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com:8500/v1/agent/reload"

# Verify services persist
curl --cacert /etc/letsencrypt/live/lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com/chain.pem \
  "https://lambda1.aiplus.perifery.com:8500/v1/catalog/services" | jq
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Expected Results</strong>: All previously registered services re=
main listed.</p>
